  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because$ Surface tension $(T)=$ Work done per unit area\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\\therefore \\quad T &=\\frac{d W}{d A} \\\\\r\n&=\\frac{F \\cdot d x}{d A} \\quad\\left(\\mathrm{FL}^{-1}=\\mathrm{MT}^{-2}\\right.\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$\r\n$\\therefore$ Dimension of surface tension $=\\mathrm{ML}^{2} \\mathrm{T}^{-2}$",
    "image": null
